PARETO FRONTIER (which gates conflict, with numbers):
  F1 spark-vs-spark: yeobo s7 in [0.9062,0.9707] over all 56 new points, NEVER <0.9; leveler-invariant
     (cap 8->12, pre 1.00->1.10, atk 12->40 move s7 by <=0.03). annyeong s11 in [0.8765,0.9845].
     Anti-correlated: sib+ cools ye s7 0.9429->0.9080 but heats an s11 0.8793->0.9801 (cap8/pre1.05).
     Best joint spark point is P0 itself (0.9463/0.9304) -- still double-RED.
  F2 RMS(yeobo>=0.10) vs SPARK: yeobo RMS>=0.10 needs cap8 rescue (0.118-0.126); at cap12 it is
     0.094-0.096 RAW FAIL (P0 0.0961, -0.35dB). But cap8 always fires annyeong cohviol=1 AND leaves s11 RED.
  F3 COHVIOL(b11<=4dB) vs SPARK(s11<0.9): b11 needs >=+4dB tail lift (cap>=10 rescue); the same lift
     pushes the s11 onset to 0.94+. At cap8 the lift collapses and b11 step fires (-6.05 class, cv=1).
  F4 RMS(annyeong>=0.10) vs CAP: cap12/pre1.10 gives 0.1010 (+0.09dB: sub-error-bar, fails 2x margin which
     needs >=0.1122); cap8 gives 0.104-0.109 but with cohviol=1. No corner gives RMS+margin AND cv=0 AND spark<0.9.
  Structural cause (confirms 29.2 Round-4): coherence peakcap (0.9/peak, +-6dB) + Gc rescale re-pin tail
  onsets to ~0.9 under EVERY setting; one scalar gain per segment cannot satisfy RMS-fill (+6dB needed)
  and spark-avoidance (binds at +5.3dB) simultaneously. Parametric search cannot cross this; it is not a tuning gap.

